      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Ref: 8914\n\nSuperb Three-Bedroom Bungalow with Detached Garage On C. 0.9 Acres of Mature Gardens (With Development Potential) For Sale By Private Treaty\n\nLOCATION & DESCRIPTION: \nQUINN Property are delighted to present this superb three-bedroom bungalow to the market. Set amidst the rolling countryside of County Wicklow, Redcross offers a wonderful blend of tranquility, village character and accessibility with amenities to include a village shop, school, pub, brewery and restaurant. Ideally positioned close to the picturesque village of Avoca, the Meeting of the Waters and the beautiful beaches of Brittas Bay, the area offers an abundance of opportunities to enjoy the great outdoors. Arklow is just 11km away, with Rathnew approximately 14km, while convenient access to the nearby M11 allows South Dublin to be reached within an hour, making this an appealing location for those seeking a peaceful setting without compromising on connectivity.\n\nThis bright and spacious family home offers expansive accommodation throughout and presents an excellent opportunity for those looking to modernise and make the property their own. The living accommodation is thoughtfully laid out, with a generous living room to the left leading through to an open-plan kitchen/dining area and adjoining sunroom. These rooms benefit from an open plan living concept however have the benefit of either sliding doors or patio doors which can be closed to enhance privacy as and when needed. The property further comprises a family bathroom and three well-proportioned bedrooms, one of which benefits from an ensuite. The floored attic now provides excellent additional storage space but could be adapted for use as a study, hobby room, children`s playroom or additional bedrooms depending on your needs. This adds to the home`s practicality.`\n\nAccommodation comprises as follows:\nEntrance Hall:3.90m x 7.57mCarpet flooring, stairs to first floor, under stairs storage. \nLiving Room:4.27m x 5.04mCarpet flooring, feature fireplace with stove, abundance of natural light.\nKitchen/Dining Room:4.03m x 8.09mMix of laminate and tiled flooring, fitted eye and waist level units, tiled splash back, extractor fan, plumbed for washing machine, abundance of natural light. \nSun Room:4.45m x 3.67mLaminate flooring, doors to rear garden. \nUtility Room:1.97m x 1.71mTiled flooring.\nBathroom:2.92m x 1.63mFully tiled, W.C., W.H.B., bath. \nBedroom 3:2.92m x 3.52mCarpet flooring.\nBedroom 1:4.02m x 3.78mCarpet flooring, built in wardrobe, garden views. \nEn-Suite:2.92m x 0.95mFully tiled, W.C., W.H.B., electric shower.\nBedroom 2:3.03m x 4.73mLaminate flooring, abundance of natural light.\nAttic Room:4.87m x 14.53mSuitable for storage but adaptable for alternative uses.\n\nOUTSIDE:\nExternally, the property is approached via a generous tarmacadam driveway which wraps around the house, with mature hedging providing excellent privacy. There are well-maintained lawned areas to the side and rear, along with a detached block-built garage benefiting from two entrances. \n\nTo the rear, the property enjoys a large parcel of land, offering excellent potential for a variety of uses and, subject to the necessary planning permission, possible future development potential.\n\nSERVICES AND FEATURES:\nAll Mains Services\nOil Fired Central Heating\nProperty Extends To: C. 138m2 \nAttic Space Extends To. C: 75m2\nBuilt: 1997\n\nBER DETAILS:\nBER: C1\nBER No. 107306011\nEnergy Performance Indicator: 154.23 kWh/m²/yr\n\nA Wonderful Wicklow Setting with Endless Possibilities\n"
